// =============================================================================
// Scalable Multi-Tenant B2B SaaS EMR & ERP — Prisma Schema
// Version      : 2026-06-15.v1
// Architecture : Shared-Tables + PostgreSQL Row-Level Security (RLS)
// Standards    : UUIDv4 PKs · Soft Deletes · Audit-ready · Optimised Indexes
// =============================================================================
//
// MULTI-TENANCY STRATEGY — DECISION LOG
// ──────────────────────────────────────
// Option A: Schema-per-tenant  → Total isolation, prohibitive ops cost at scale
// Option B: DB-per-tenant      → Maximum isolation, unworkable at SaaS scale
// Option C: Shared + tenant_id → Cost-efficient, horizontally scalable          ← CHOSEN
//
// Decision: Shared tables with `tenant_id UUID NOT NULL` on every row, enforced
// by PostgreSQL Row-Level Security (RLS). The application layer sets
// `SET LOCAL app.current_tenant_id = '<uuid>'` inside every transaction via a
// Prisma middleware. Each policy: `USING (tenant_id = current_setting('app.current_tenant_id')::uuid)`
//
// CHALLENGER REVIEW — resolved weaknesses:
//   ① Money columns: Decimal(18,4) — NOT Float. Avoids IEEE-754 rounding in billing.
//   ② Roles: junction table (UserRoleAssignment) — NOT an array column. Enables
//     per-role indexing, grant/revoke auditing, and future per-role expiry.
//   ③ PrivilegedAccessGrant: own table — NOT JSONB on platform_tenants. Required
//     for expiry-based cron queries and status index.
//   ④ audit_entries: append-only enforced by DB trigger (see migration notes).
//     No `updated_at`; adding one would invite accidental mutation.
//   ⑤ OutboxEvent: partial indexes on (status, created_at) for processor hotpath.
//   ⑥ EMR embedded arrays (diagnoses/medications/observations): JSONB is correct
//     here — they are always loaded together per encounter and never queried
//     individually across encounters.
//   ⑦ Subscription split: ClinicSubscription (patient packages inside clinic) is
//     separate from PlatformSubscription (SaaS billing at operator level).
// =============================================================================

generator client {
  provider = "prisma-client-js"
  output   = "../node_modules/.prisma/client"
}

datasource db {
  provider = "postgresql"
  url      = env("DATABASE_URL")
}

